            chapterProgress: 'Section 1 — Supercharge Challenge',
            conceptText: `Push your React skills to the next level with advanced component patterns.

In this challenge, you'll implement:
- Higher-Order Components (HOCs)
- Render Props pattern
- Compound Components pattern

These patterns help you create more flexible and reusable components.

Higher-Order Component: A function that takes a component and returns a new component with enhanced functionality.

Render Props: A technique where a component receives a function as a prop that returns a React element.

Compound Components: Components that work together to form a complete UI, sharing implicit state.`,
            instructions: `Create a compound component system for a Tabs component:
  • Tabs (parent component managing state)
  • TabList (container for tab buttons)
  • Tab (individual tab button)
  • TabPanels (container for panels)
  • TabPanel (individual panel content)

The components should share state implicitly and work together seamlessly.`,
